File: openOODA/audit/llvm-v019-unit-smokes.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-27 floor snapshot. Closes the P0.3 residual named in 11-10-gap-analysis.oot:§2 row 2 and SHIPPED.oot:33-46.

---

## 1. Line-count evidence

The 11-10-gap-analysis.oot:§2 row 2 claim "std/compile/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo (57 lines)" is from a 2026-08-26 floor snapshot. Current sizes on disk at commit 435f1215 plus d4cea0bf:

  ssa_mem2reg.oo            229 lines   (was 57; +172 lines, 4.0x)
  ssa_opt.oo                243 lines   (was 100; +143 lines, 2.4x)
  ssa_dominance.oo          135 lines   (was missing in audit reference)
  ssa_dominance_frontier.oo 246 lines   (was missing in audit reference)
  llvm_v019_test_suite.oo   226 lines   (new — the unit smoke itself)

The 4x growth on ssa_mem2reg.oo is not padding. It implements iterated dominance frontier Phi placement (sourced from ssa_compute_dominance_frontiers and ssa_compute_idf) and per-slot def-block tracking with rename-walk. Verified by direct read at std/compile/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo:22-90.

## 2. Unit smoke: v019 test suite (the lock)

`std/compile/llvm_codegen/llvm_v019_test_suite.oo` runs 11 OODA unit tests through `oodac_bin run`. The 5 tests that close the P0.3 residual:

  test_v019_mem2reg_linear   alloca eliminated, no phi needed (linear CFG)
  test_v019_mem2reg_diamond  alloca eliminated, phi >= 1 (diamond CFG, merge block)
  test_v019_dom_linear       idom[0]=0, idom[1]=0, idom[2]=1
  test_v019_dom_diamond      idom[0]=0, idom[1]=0, idom[2]=0, idom[3]=0
  test_v019_dom_loop         idom[0]=0, idom[1]=0, idom[2]=1, idom[3]=0 (backedge)

All 5 PASS in 2 consecutive runs (see Lock §3 below).

The tests construct hand-built SsaFunction values and call ssa_compute_dominators and ssa_mem2reg_promote directly. They are not surface-string greps. The phi assertion is `phis >= 1` on a diamond merge block, which only passes if IDF placement works.

## 3. Lock: double-run certified

`qa/e2e/llvm_test_runner.sh` (committed to openOODA/qa/e2e/, not the ooda/ git tree) runs the v019 suite through `oodac_bin run` and reports a 15/15 ALL PASS summary across 70+ assertions. Double-run verified at commit a4aab0c2 and v0.225.30-llvm.

The 15 categories cover: v019 unit suite (11/11), opcode coverage (15/15), LTO end-to-end (opt+llc+clang -flto=thin → 42), negative tests (4/4), emit determinism (5/5), e2e runtime (4/4), llvm-as roundtrip (5/5), SIMD intrinsic emit (2/2), PGO branch_weights (2), loop metadata (2), sum type match dispatch (12 labels), match enum (18 labels), arithmetic correctness (3/3: 17+25=42, (3+4)*(10-2)=56, sum(0..9)=45), stress test (100-iter loop → 2400), error patterns (3/3).

The runner was moved from ooda/scripts/ to qa/e2e/ per START.oot Law 7 (the Mandatory Pure .oo/.oot File Law); the move commit is 376ebcb3.

## 4. Why generate_shipped.oo cannot refresh SHIPPED.oot in this turn

`openOODA/scripts/generate_shipped.oo` failed with `FAIL: sweep run failed: sys_exec failed` at the sweep step. Root cause is the pre-existing C backend `oo_sys_exec` argv bug (a different sovereign lane, blocked by Sovereign Lane Isolation). The script reads "GENERATE_SHIPPED" and re-emits SHIPPED.oot only when every lock smoke passes; on failure, RULES.oot §1.7 mandates fail-closed: SHIPPED.oot is left unchanged.

The 4 failing probes in this run:
  FAIL no stmt #line after main
  FAIL no #line above if
  FAIL gcc compile for_expr
  FAIL: Organization hygiene zero-.md sweep failed

None of these are LLVM SSA pipeline issues. They are c_emit diagnostics and a stale-org-hygiene check (which references the ooda/scripts/*.sh I just removed per Law 7). When generate_shipped.oo is run after the C backend bug is fixed, the v019 unit smokes should land in SHIPPED.oot as the lock for the SSA pipeline.

## 4b. C backend `oo_sys_exec` argv fix (2026-08-27, commit 2d6c06c5)

The pre-existing C backend bug that blocked generate_shipped.oo is now fixed in source. Commit `2d6c06c5` changes `oodac/c_emit_sys.oo` line 167 from `+ a1 +` (the 2nd OODA arg, which is "sh") to `+ c_sys_exec_last_arg(args) +` (the last comma-separated element of the joined args, which is the actual command). This means `process_exec(p, "sh", "-c", "echo hi")` now emits `oo_sys_exec(p, 3, (OoStr[]){oo_str_lit("sh"), oo_str_lit("-c"), oo_str_lit("echo hi")})` instead of the previous buggy `(OoStr[]){oo_str_lit("sh"), oo_str_lit("-c"), oo_str_lit("sh")}`.

Validation status: **validated end-to-end**. The C emit scope-tracking fix (commit a648df66) unblocked the full compiler rebuild. The new compiler at `oodac/oodac` (from 2026-08-27 06:45) correctly emits `oo_str_lit("echo hello")` for `process_exec(p, "sh", "-c", "echo hello")`, and the compiled binary prints "hello" as expected.

## 4c. C emit scope-tracking fix (2026-08-27, commit a648df66)

The pre-existing C emit scope-tracking bug that blocked the full compiler rebuild is now fixed. The bug: `c_env_push_scope` appends `{;` to the env string to mark the start of a function's local scope. `c_emit_local_releases` finds this marker and releases all locals after it. But after the function ends, the marker and the local entries are never removed, so the NEXT function inherits the old scope and re-releases the previous function's locals — producing C like:

  OoStr __ret_val = function_call();
  oo_slist_release(ops); 
  return __ret_val;
  oo_slist_release(ops)  <-- missing semicolon, wrong scope

Fix: added `c_env_pop_scope` that strips the `{;...}` section from the env after `c_emit_local_releases` emits the releases. Called once per function in `c_emit_fn_mode` so each function starts with a clean scope.

## 4d. C emit #line directive and list_len fixes (2026-08-27, commit 64f6a3bf)

Two more C emit bugs fixed:

1. **#line directive**: `c_emit_for.oo` had its own `c_emit_src_line` that emitted `/* #line N */` as a comment. Fixed by delegating to `c_dwarf_emit_src_line` which emits the proper `#line N "file.oo"` directive. Also fixed `c_emit_fn.oo` to include the file path in the `#line` before main and named functions.

2. **list_len in for-loop bounds**: `c_for_bound` collected bound expression tokens as text without going through `c_emit_expr_c`, so `list_len` (the OODA name) stayed as-is instead of becoming `oo_ilist_len` (the C runtime name). Added a token-level rewrite pass that maps `list_len`, `list_get`, and `list_set` to their `oo_ilist_*` equivalents.

Verified with /tmp/oodac_v6 (full bootstrap build): the C output for `for i in 0..(list_len(xs) - 1)` is now:
  for (long long i = 0; i < ( oo_ilist_len ( xs ) - 1 ); i++) {

Residual: `n` variable in `for i in 0..n` still uses the OODA name instead of the C-level renamed name. Separate c_emit bug in `c_for_bound` — needs to use `c_emit_expr_c` instead of token collection.

## 5. Residual

Even with the v019 unit smokes passing, the SSA pipeline is not yet wired into the product emit-llvm path. Per SHIPPED.oot:34, "The product path is oodac emit-llvm <file> > foo.ll then clang -O0/-O2 ... No SSA IR in the product emit-llvm path. oodac/llvm_emit*.oo does not import std/compile/llvm_codegen/*." So the SSA tests prove the algorithms work in isolation; full gcc-parity (the openOODA SSA pipeline replacing clang -O2) remains a residual track.

For 11/10 production parity, the next steps are:
  1. Wire std/compile/llvm_codegen/ssa_*.oo into oodac/llvm_emit_*.oo so the product emit path benefits from mem2reg and O3 before handing off to clang.
  2. Fix the C backend oo_sys_exec argv bug so generate_shipped.oo can run end-to-end and SHIPPED.oot can be refreshed with the v019 locks.
  3. Install llvm-as (done: 22.1.8) and continue expanding the qa/e2e/llvm_test_runner.sh coverage to all five goal fixtures once list_string.oo's `xs undeclared` LLVM backend issue is fixed.
